# Environment variable NAMES used by the website. This file holds names only; never put a real value here.
# Real values live in the hosting provider's settings (Vercel project settings) and, for local work, in an
# untracked file named .env.local, which .gitignore already excludes.

# ---- Existing website configuration (all optional; the site has safe defaults) -----------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_PHONE=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ECOMMERCE_LICENCE_NUMBER=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# ---- Business platform: Supabase (PLAT-0001; nothing in the site reads these yet) --------------------------------
# Leave these unset until a Supabase project for DEVELOPMENT has been approved. Use a separate project for
# production, with its own keys (REC-PLAT-012). With them unset, the public quotation flow behaves as it does today.
#
# The project URL and the anon (publishable) key are designed to reach browsers. Row level security is what protects
# the data, which is why the migrations are tested for it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# The service-role key bypasses row level security. Server only: never give it a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name, never import it
# from a client component, never commit it. No code in this phase uses it; do not set it anywhere yet.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---- Customer accounts (PLAT-0002): OFF by default and absent from the public site unless switched on ---------------
# A SERVER variable (never NEXT_PUBLIC_). The account routes answer 404 unless this is exactly "true". It is ignored on
# a production deployment (VERCEL_ENV=production), so it cannot open public accounts by accident. Use it for local
# work and for preview deployments only, with a DEVELOPMENT Supabase project.
# CUSTOMER_ACCOUNTS_ENABLED=
#
# The public origin that links in sign-in emails point back to (for a preview deployment). Not needed on localhost.
# CUSTOMER_ACCOUNTS_SITE_URL=
#
# Optional. A short sentence shown as a banner on every account page, for example "Local preview: demonstration data".
# Use it whenever the data behind the pages is not real, so a demonstration can never pass for the real thing.
# CUSTOMER_ACCOUNTS_PREVIEW_LABEL=
